#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e9abbc-b0b5-51a6-b23b-a32a027382f3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing an Expression Raised to an Odd Power"}] :question/id #uuid "20f6391d-7ada-51b2-a384-f12a31a622c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8053" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $5(x-6)^7 = 640$." :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x-6)^7$ term and then taking the $7$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x-6)^7$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5(x - 6)^{7} &= 640 \\\\\n(x - 6)^{7} &= 128\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $7$th root of each side and solve for $x$. Since $n=7$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 6)^{7} &= 128 \\\\\n\\sqrt[7]{(x - 6)^{7}} &= \\sqrt[7]{128} \\\\\nx - 6 &= \\sqrt[7]{2^{7}} \\\\\nx - 6 &= 2 \\\\\nx &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=8$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98f98657-c9c6-5b38-825c-992bcf28d9e3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Odd Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "26f0aea2-1440-5e96-9013-8238214b4966" :question/math-academy-id "e-8065" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $96x^5=3$." :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $x^5$ term and then taking the $5$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $x^5$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n96x^{5} &= 3 \\\\\nx^{5} &= \\frac{1}{32}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $5$th root of each side and solve for $x$. Since $n=5$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{5} &= \\frac{1}{32} \\\\\n\\sqrt[5]{x^{5}} &= \\sqrt[5]{\\frac{1}{32}} \\\\\nx &= \\sqrt[5]{(\\frac{1}{2})^{5}} \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac12\n$$"}]}
